{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeNPp4pnpFBbTzTpoJswJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Tdihs9Y91rNAd6YPKEaUoc","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kubernetes/website/main/content/en/docs/tasks/administer-cluster/reserve-compute-resources.md","prompt":"Extract, with short direct quotes from the source, the following: (1) the opening paragraph about node capacity and the fact that Kubernetes nodes can be scheduled to Capacity and pods can consume all available capacity by default, which is an issue because nodes typically run OS system daemons and Kubernetes system daemons; (2) the definition of Node Allocatable as the amount of compute resources available for pods; (3) the definition of `kube-reserved` — what it is meant to capture (resource reservation for Kubernetes system daemons like the kubelet, container runtime, node problem detector, etc.), and that it is not meant to reserve resources for system daemons that run as pods; (4) the definition of `system-reserved` — what it is meant to capture (resource reservation for OS system daemons like sshd, udev; should reserve kernel memory; reserving resources for user login sessions is recommended); (5) any statement about eviction thresholds (`--eviction-hard`) reserving memory; (6) any TEXT (non-image) statement of how Capacity, kube-reserved, system-reserved, eviction-threshold and Allocatable relate — for example a sentence or equation such as \"Allocatable = Capacity - kube-reserved - system-reserved - eviction-threshold\". If the relationship appears ONLY as an image/diagram with no textual equivalent, say so explicitly. Quote exact source wording and name the section heading for each."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":213,"cache_read_input_tokens":117569,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_i