{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeNPrXnpcPhxDE3QJcP9k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RdDHMh4Yq7hc4zr9hAYMNW","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kubernetes/website/main/content/en/docs/concepts/policy/limit-range.md","prompt":"Extract with short direct quotes, in source order, the complete \"Constraints on resource limits and requests\" list — every bullet/numbered item exactly as written. I expect items along the lines of: the LimitRange administrator creates a LimitRange in a namespace; users create/update/patch resources in the namespace; the admission controller applies default request/limit values for any Pod/Container that does not set compute resource requirements; the request/limit is tracked to ensure it does not exceed max/min in any LimitRange present in the namespace; if a violation occurs the API server rejects the request with HTTP status code 403 FORBIDDEN and a message explaining the constraint violated; if a LimitRange is activated in a namespace for compute resources like cpu and memory, users must specify requests or limits for those values (otherwise the system may reject Pod creation); the statement that LimitRange validations occur only at Pod admission stage and not on running Pods; and the note about multiple LimitRange objects in the same namespace producing non-deterministic results. Also quote any \"Note:\" or \"Caution:\" callouts on the page. Quote exact source wording."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4026,"cache_read_input_tokens":117782,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4026},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78cbcb15-0318-4f05-91e9-c43691