{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0184NPzUJ9k18LtpRrVENX4x","type":"tool_result","content":"# Resource Quota Operating Principles and Configuration\n\n## How ResourceQuota Operates (\"How Kubernetes ResourceQuotas work\")\n\n- \"A cluster administrator creates at least one ResourceQuota for each namespace.\"\n- \"Users create resources (pods, services, etc.) in the namespace, and the quota system tracks usage to ensure it does not exceed hard resource limits.\"\n- \"If creating or updating a resource violates a quota constraint, the control plane rejects that request with HTTP status code `403 Forbidden`.\"\n- \"If quotas are enabled in a namespace for resource such as `cpu` and `memory`, users must specify requests or limits for those values when they define a Pod.\"\n\n## ResourceQuota Enablement (\"Enabling Resource Quota\")\n\n\"ResourceQuota support is enabled by default for many Kubernetes distributions. It is enabled when the API server `--enable-admission-plugins=` flag has `ResourceQuota` as one of its arguments.\"\n\n\"A resource quota is enforced in a particular namespace when there is a ResourceQuota in that namespace.\"\n\n## Compute Resource Quotas (\"Compute Resource Quota\")\n\nSupported resource types: `limits.cpu`, `limits.memory`, `requests.cpu`, `requests.memory`, `hugepages-<size>`, `cpu`, `memory`\n\n## Storage Resource Quotas (\"Quota for storage\")\n\nSupported resource types: `requests.storage`, `persistentvolumeclaims`, `<storage-class-name>.storageclass.storage.k8s.io/requests.storage`, `<storage-class-name>.storageclass.storage.k8s.io/persistentvolumeclaims`\n\n## Object Count Quota Syntax (\"Quota on object count\")\n\n- `count/<resource>.<group>` for non-core API groups\n- `count/<resource>` for core API group resources\n\nCountable resources: `count/pods`, `count/persistentvolumeclaims`, `count/services`, `count/secrets`, `count/configmaps`, `count/deployments.apps`, `count/replicasets.apps`, `count/statefulsets.apps`, `count/jobs.batch`, `count/cronjobs.batch`\n\n## Quota and Capacity Relationship (\"Quota and Cluster Capacity\")\n\n\"ResourceQuotas are independent of the cluster capacity...if you add nodes to your cluster, this does *not* automatically give each namespace the ability to consume more resources.\"\n\n## Default Enforcement (\"How Kubernetes ResourceQuotas work\")\n\n\"You can use a LimitRange to automatically set a default request for these resources.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78cbcb15-0318-4f05-91e9-c436917333d0","uuid":"230e7ad8-0f75-46f9-acb8-3f08fa8b9d36","timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:53:40.922Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":31077,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Resource Quota Operating Principles and Configuration\n\n## How ResourceQuota Operates (\"How Kubernetes ResourceQuotas work\")\n\n- \"A cluster administrator creates at least one ResourceQuota for each namespace.\"\n- \"Users create resources (pods, services, etc.) in the namespace, and the quota system tracks usage to ensure it does not exceed hard resource limits.\"\n- \"If creating or updating a resource violates a quota constraint, the control plane rejects that request with HTTP status code `403 Forbidden`.\"\n- \"If quotas are enabled in a namespace for resource such as `cpu` and `memory`, users must specify requests or limits for those values when they define a Pod.\"\n\n## ResourceQuota Enablement (\"Enabling Resource Quota\")\n\n\"ResourceQuota support is enabled by default for many Kubernetes distributions. It is enabled when the API server `--enable-admission-plugins=` flag has `ResourceQuota` as one of its arguments.\"\n\n\"A resource quota is enforced in a particular namespace when there is a ResourceQuota in that namespace.\"\n\n## Compute Resource Quotas (\"Compute Resource Quota\")\n\nSupported resource types: `limits.cpu`, `limits.memory`, `requests.cpu`, `requests.memory`, `hugepages-<size>`, `cpu`, `memory`\n\n## Storage Resource Quotas (\"Quota for storage\")\n\nSupported resource types: `requests.storage`, `persistentvolumeclaims`, `<storage-class-name>.storageclass.storage.k8s.io/requests.storage`, `<storage-class-name>.storageclass.storage.k8s.io/persistentvolumeclaims`\n\n## Object Count Quota Syntax (\"Quota on object count\")\n\n- `count/<resource>.<group>` for non-core API groups\n- `count/<resource>` for core API group resources\n\nCountable resources: `count/pods`, `count/persistentvolumeclaims`, `count/services`, `count/secrets`, `count/configmaps`, `count/deployments.apps`, `count/replicasets.apps`, `count/statefulsets.apps`, `count/jobs.batch`, `count/cronjobs.batch`\n\n## Quota and Capacity Relationship (\"Quota and Cluster Capacity\")\n\n\"ResourceQuotas are independent of the cluster capacity...if you add nodes to your cluster, this does *not* automatically give each namespace the ability to consume more resources.\"\n\n## Default Enforcement (\"How Kubernetes ResourceQuotas work\")\n\n\"You can use a LimitRange to automatically set a default request for these resources.\"","durationMs":7061,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kubernetes/website/main/content/en/docs/concepts/policy/resource-quotas.md"}}
