{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019gAHADNag5uZFKadvpgAvB","type":"tool_result","content":"# Extracted Details from Kubernetes API Access Control Page\n\n**(1) Diagram alt-text/caption:**\n\"Diagram of request handling steps for Kubernetes API request\" (from overview section)\n\n**(2) Authorization modules statement:**\nFrom Authorization section: \"Kubernetes supports multiple authorization modules, such as ABAC mode, RBAC Mode, and Webhook mode.\" Additionally: \"if any module authorizes the request, then the request can proceed. If all of the modules deny the request, then the request is denied.\"\n\n**(3) Admission Control sequence:**\nFrom Admission Control section: \"When multiple admission controllers are configured, they are called in order.\"\n\n**(4) Admission Control modification capability:**\nFrom Admission Control section: \"admission controllers can also set complex defaults for fields.\"\n\n**(5) Transport security port and TLS details:**\nFrom Transport security section: \"the Kubernetes API server listens on port 6443 on the first non-localhost network interface, protected by TLS.\" Also: \"you need a copy of that CA certificate configured into your `~/.kube/config`\"\n\n**(6) API server ports and IPs section:**\n**This section does not exist as a separate heading.** Port and binding information appears within the Transport security section only."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78cbcb15-0318-4f05-91e9-c436917333d0","uuid":"97e08a35-b5a8-4bd3-968c-2fe317c3dfef","timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:54:11.075Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":8373,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Extracted Details from Kubernetes API Access Control Page\n\n**(1) Diagram alt-text/caption:**\n\"Diagram of request handling steps for Kubernetes API request\" (from overview section)\n\n**(2) Authorization modules statement:**\nFrom Authorization section: \"Kubernetes supports multiple authorization modules, such as ABAC mode, RBAC Mode, and Webhook mode.\" Additionally: \"if any module authorizes the request, then the request can proceed. If all of the modules deny the request, then the request is denied.\"\n\n**(3) Admission Control sequence:**\nFrom Admission Control section: \"When multiple admission controllers are configured, they are called in order.\"\n\n**(4) Admission Control modification capability:**\nFrom Admission Control section: \"admission controllers can also set complex defaults for fields.\"\n\n**(5) Transport security port and TLS details:**\nFrom Transport security section: \"the Kubernetes API server listens on port 6443 on the first non-localhost network interface, protected by TLS.\" Also: \"you need a copy of that CA certificate configured into your `~/.kube/config`\"\n\n**(6) API server ports and IPs section:**\n**This section does not exist as a separate heading.** Port and binding information appears within the Transport security section only.","durationMs":3781,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kubernetes/website/main/content/en/docs/concepts/security/controlling-access.md"}}
