{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wup9ZSXiQwF2PAfFc16V5X","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tsource_url: \"https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/labels-annotations-taints/\"\n3\tsource_raw: \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kubernetes/website/main/content/en/docs/reference/labels-annotations-taints/_index.md\"\n4\tfetched_at: \"2026-08-24T09:52:00-0400\"\n5\tauthority: \"Kubernetes project (kubernetes.io/docs), CC BY 4.0\"\n6\tobjectives_covered: [\"D1.3\"]\n7\tconcepts_covered: [\"standard-node-labels\", \"node-labels\", \"topology-key\"]\n8\tscope_note: \"Targeted extraction of six entries only, to source §3's 'Kubernetes populates a standard set of labels on all nodes' claim with actual label names. The full reference page is very large and was not cached wholesale.\"\n9\t---\n10\t# Well-Known Labels, Annotations and Taints — selected node entries (kubernetes.io/docs/reference/labels-annotations-taints/)\n11\t\n12\t> **Extraction note.** This page is a reference list with terse entries. Only\n13\t> `kubernetes.io/hostname` was returned as a clean **[VERBATIM]** description sentence.\n14\t> The remaining entries are **[PARTIAL]** — the label keys and their \"Used on\" targets are\n15\t> confirmed, but the description wording was condensed by the fetch. **Cite the label\n16\t> keys from this file; do not quote the [PARTIAL] descriptions as source sentences.**\n17\t\n18\t## `kubernetes.io/hostname`\n19\t\n20\t- Used on: Node\n21\t- **[VERBATIM]** — \"The Kubelet populates this label with the hostname of the node.\"\n22\t\n23\t## `topology.kubernetes.io/zone`\n24\t\n25\t- Used on: Node, PersistentVolume\n26\t- **[PARTIAL]** — \"A zone represents a logical failure domain\"; populated by the kubelet\n27\t  or cloud-controller-manager.\n28\t\n29\t## `topology.kubernetes.io/region`\n30\t\n31\t- Used on: Node, PersistentVolume\n32\t- **[PARTIAL]** — cross-references the `topology.kubernetes.io/zone` entry; a region is a\n33\t  larger domain made up of zones.\n34\t\n35\t## `kubernetes.io/os` and `kubernetes.io/arch`\n36\t\n37\t- Used on: Node (and Pod, for `kubernetes.io/os`)\n38\t- **[PARTIAL]** — the kubelet populates these from the Go runtime values `runtime.GOOS`\n39\t  and `runtime.GOARCH`, to support heterogeneous clusters.\n40\t\n41\t## `node.kubernetes.io/unschedulable` (taint)\n42\t\n43\t- **[PARTIAL]** — \"The taint will be added to a node when initializing the node to avoid\n44\t  race condition.\"\n45\t\n46\t---\n47\t\n48\tNOT IN THIS SNAPSHOT: the `node-restriction.kubernetes.io/` prefix entry was not returned\n49\tby this fetch. **It is not a gap** — that fact is already cached verbatim in\n50\t`k8s-docs-assign-pod-node-2026-08-23.md`: \"the NodeRestriction admission plugin prevents\n51\tthe kubelet from setting labels with a node-restriction.kubernetes.io/ prefix.\" Cite that\n52\tfile for §3's forward-bearing to Chapter 8.\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78cbcb15-0318-4f05-91e9-c436917333d0","uuid":"99c31995-c24a-4c59-82c1-55c8e33a8053","timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:58:10.164Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\sources\\k8s-docs-well-known-labels-2026-08-24.md","content":"---\nsource_url: \"https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/labels-annotations-taints/\"\nsource_raw: \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kubernetes/website/main/content/en/docs/reference/labels-annotations-taints/_index.md\"\nfetched_at: \"2026-08-24T09:52:00-0400\"\nauthority: \"Kubernetes project (kubernetes.io/docs), CC BY 4.0\"\nobjectives_covered: [\"D1.3\"]\nconcepts_covered: [\"standard-node-labels\", \"node-labels\", \"topology-key\"]\nscope_note: \"Targeted extraction of six entries only, to source §3's 'Kubernetes populates a standard set of labels on all nodes' claim with actual label names. The full reference page is very large and was not cached wholesale.\"\n---\n# Well-Known Labels, Annotations and Taints — selected node entries (kubernetes.io/docs/reference/labels-annotations-taints/)\n\n> **Extraction note.** This page is a reference list with terse entries. Only\n> `kubernetes.io/hostname` was returned as a clean **[VERBATIM]** description sentence.\n> The remaining entries are **[PARTIAL]** — the label keys and their \"Used on\" targets are\n> confirmed, but the description wording was condensed by the fetch. **Cite the label\n> keys from this file; do not quote the [PARTIAL] descriptions as source sentences.**\n\n## `kubernetes.io/hostname`\n\n- Used on: Node\n- **[VERBATIM]** — \"The Kubelet populates this label with the hostname of the node.\"\n\n## `topology.kubernetes.io/zone`\n\n- Used on: Node, PersistentVolume\n- **[PARTIAL]** — \"A zone represents a logical failure domain\"; populated by the kubelet\n  or cloud-controller-manager.\n\n## `topology.kubernetes.io/region`\n\n- Used on: Node, PersistentVolume\n- **[PARTIAL]** — cross-references the `topology.kubernetes.io/zone` entry; a region is a\n  larger domain made up of zones.\n\n## `kubernetes.io/os` and `kubernetes.io/arch`\n\n- Used on: Node (and Pod, for `kubernetes.io/os`)\n- **[PARTIAL]** — the kubelet populates these from the Go runtime values `runtime.GOOS`\n  and `runtime.GOARCH`, to support heterogeneous clusters.\n\n## `node.kubernetes.io/unschedulable` (taint)\n\n- **[PARTIAL]** — \"The taint will be added to a node when initializing the node to avoid\n  race condition.\"\n\n---\n\nNOT IN THIS SNAPSHOT: the `node-restriction.kubernetes.io/` prefix entry was not returned\nby this fetch. **It is not a gap** — that fact is already cached verbatim in\n`k8s-docs-assign-pod-node-2026-08-23.md`: \"the NodeRestriction admission plugin prevents\nthe kubelet from setting labels with a node-restriction.kubernetes.io/ prefix.\" Cite that\nfile for §3's forward-bearing to Chapter 8.\n","numLines":53,"startLine":1,"totalLines":53}}}
