{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013SnQ1YvGg5kVK2KTPQVMYM","type":"tool_result","content":"# Search Results\n\n**`.spec.unschedulable` field or `node.kubernetes.io/unschedulable` taint:**\nNo mentions found on this page.\n\n**Connection between `kubectl cordon` and Node object fields/taints:**\nNo explicit connection stated on this page.\n\n**(a) Manual Node administration paragraph:**\n\"Marking a node as unschedulable prevents the scheduler from placing new pods onto that Node but does not affect existing Pods on the Node. This is useful as a preparatory step before a node reboot or other maintenance. To mark a Node unschedulable, run: `kubectl cordon $NODENAME`\"\n\n**(b) DaemonSet Pods and unschedulable Nodes:**\n\"Pods that are part of a DaemonSet tolerate being run on an unschedulable Node. DaemonSets typically provide node-local services that should run on the Node even if it is being drained of workload applications.\"\n\n**(c) `Ready` condition with three values including Unknown:**\nNot found on this page.\n\n**(d) Default value/duration for node-monitor-grace-period:**\nNot mentioned on this page."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78cbcb15-0318-4f05-91e9-c436917333d0","uuid":"24c79a2c-4c83-4606-8231-c733b3539829","timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:59:28.233Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":14884,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Search Results\n\n**`.spec.unschedulable` field or `node.kubernetes.io/unschedulable` taint:**\nNo mentions found on this page.\n\n**Connection between `kubectl cordon` and Node object fields/taints:**\nNo explicit connection stated on this page.\n\n**(a) Manual Node administration paragraph:**\n\"Marking a node as unschedulable prevents the scheduler from placing new pods onto that Node but does not affect existing Pods on the Node. This is useful as a preparatory step before a node reboot or other maintenance. To mark a Node unschedulable, run: `kubectl cordon $NODENAME`\"\n\n**(b) DaemonSet Pods and unschedulable Nodes:**\n\"Pods that are part of a DaemonSet tolerate being run on an unschedulable Node. DaemonSets typically provide node-local services that should run on the Node even if it is being drained of workload applications.\"\n\n**(c) `Ready` condition with three values including Unknown:**\nNot found on this page.\n\n**(d) Default value/duration for node-monitor-grace-period:**\nNot mentioned on this page.","durationMs":3599,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kubernetes/website/main/content/en/docs/concepts/architecture/nodes.md"}}
