{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0111v5NmaWF7wsddJQM9JHYK","type":"tool_result","content":"# Node Status Content Analysis\n\nThe page provided does **not contain the Conditions table** you requested. \n\nThe \"Node status\" section only states:\n\n> \"A Node's status contains the following information: * [Addresses](/docs/reference/node/node-status/#addresses) * [Conditions](/docs/reference/node/node-status/#condition) * [Capacity and Allocatable](/docs/reference/node/node-status/#capacity) * [Info](/docs/reference/node/node-status/#info)\"\n\nIt also includes:\n\n> \"You can use `kubectl` to view a Node's status and other details: ```shell kubectl describe node <insert-node-name-here> ```\"\n\nThe **\"Node heartbeats\" section** states:\n\n> \"Heartbeats, sent by Kubernetes nodes, help your cluster determine the availability of each node, and to take action when failures are detected. For nodes there are two forms of heartbeats: * Updates to the [`.status`](/docs/reference/node/node-status/) of a Node. * [Lease](/docs/concepts/architecture/leases/) objects within the `kube-node-lease` {{< glossary_tooltip term_id=\"namespace\" text=\"namespace\">}}.\"\n\nThe detailed conditions descriptions (Ready, DiskPressure, etc.) are **referenced but not included** on this page—they're linked to external documentation."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78cbcb15-0318-4f05-91e9-c436917333d0","uuid":"de0c1741-e3ba-4d93-a774-db729412afbc","timestamp":"2026-08-24T23:00:18.443Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":14884,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Node Status Content Analysis\n\nThe page provided does **not contain the Conditions table** you requested. \n\nThe \"Node status\" section only states:\n\n> \"A Node's status contains the following information: * [Addresses](/docs/reference/node/node-status/#addresses) * [Conditions](/docs/reference/node/node-status/#condition) * [Capacity and Allocatable](/docs/reference/node/node-status/#capacity) * [Info](/docs/reference/node/node-status/#info)\"\n\nIt also includes:\n\n> \"You can use `kubectl` to view a Node's status and other details: ```shell kubectl describe node <insert-node-name-here> ```\"\n\nThe **\"Node heartbeats\" section** states:\n\n> \"Heartbeats, sent by Kubernetes nodes, help your cluster determine the availability of each node, and to take action when failures are detected. For nodes there are two forms of heartbeats: * Updates to the [`.status`](/docs/reference/node/node-status/) of a Node. * [Lease](/docs/concepts/architecture/leases/) objects within the `kube-node-lease` {{< glossary_tooltip term_id=\"namespace\" text=\"namespace\">}}.\"\n\nThe detailed conditions descriptions (Ready, DiskPressure, etc.) are **referenced but not included** on this page—they're linked to external documentation.","durationMs":4368,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kubernetes/website/main/content/en/docs/concepts/architecture/nodes.md"}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01U9JpfHqv8GjJe5p95CaFGA","type":"tool_result","content":"# Taint Entry: `node.kubernetes.io/unschedulable`\n\n**Type:** Taint\n\n**Example:** `node.kubernetes.io/unschedulable: \"NoSchedule\"`\n\n**Used on:** Node\n\n**Description:** \"The taint will be added to a node when initializing the node to avoid race condition.\"\n\n---\n\n## Note on `node-restriction.kubernetes.io/` prefix\n\nThe document provided does not contain any entry for a `node-restriction.kubernetes.io/` prefix. This namespace is not referenced in the well-known labels, annotations, and taints reference material shown.\n\n---\n\n## Observation\n\nThe entry indicates this taint is applied during node initialization but does not explicitly mention cordoning or manual marking as unschedulable by an operator. The description focuses on preventing race conditions during startup rather than administrative actions."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78cbcb15-0318-4f05-91e9-c436917333d0","uuid":"c257b7ca-0a6d-4056-af61-065f0f5d4d71","timestamp":"2026-08-24T23:00:19.905Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":119528,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Taint Entry: `node.kubernetes.io/unschedulable`\n\n**Type:** Taint\n\n**Example:** `node.kubernetes.io/unschedulable: \"NoSchedule\"`\n\n**Used on:** Node\n\n**Description:** \"The taint will be added to a node when initializing the node to avoid race condition.\"\n\n---\n\n## Note on `node-restriction.kubernetes.io/` prefix\n\nThe document provided does not contain any entry for a `node-restriction.kubernetes.io/` prefix. This namespace is not referenced in the well-known labels, annotations, and taints reference material shown.\n\n---\n\n## Observation\n\nThe entry indicates this taint is applied during node initialization but does not explicitly mention cordoning or manual marking as unschedulable by an operator. The description focuses on preventing race conditions during startup rather than administrative actions.","durationMs":3262,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kubernetes/website/main/content/en/docs/reference/labels-annotations-taints/_index.md"}}
