{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"\n\n> \"A LimitRange is a policy to constrain the resource allocations (limits and requests) that you can specify for each applicable object kind (such as Pod or PersistentVolumeClaim) in a namespace.\""}},"session_id":"78cbcb15-0318-4f05-91e9-c436917333d0","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"a7bbc0b5-0a11-49c1-b4cd-cbe29a61f2ba"}
{"type":"stream_event","event":{"type":"content_block_delta","index":1,"delta":{"type":"text_delta","text":"\n\n## What a LimitRange provides\n\n> \"Enforce minimum and maximum compute resources usage per Pod or Container in a namespace.\"\n\n> \"Enforce minimum and maximum storage request per PersistentVolum"}},"session_id":"78cbcb15-0318-4f05-91e9-c436917333d0","parent_tool_use_id":null,"uuid":"cab18608-f0e6-4714-9a46-7dff8e17d833"}
